extraction_notes: "Page span: the heading and lore fill printed 86 and the stats fill printed 87; printed 88 opens the Coalition War Machine chapter. GROUP: the book''s Coalition Military O.C.C.s section (printed 67), so men-of-arms and men_of_arms true. HAND TO HAND: Commando, printed as unchangeable, so the price block is empty - nothing is sold. MOS: four +15% skills from one of eight areas, modelled as skills.mos with one option per area, each a choice of four; the book''s Piloting is the Pilot category. The +15% is taken as the MOS figure in place of the ordinary category bonus. MONEY: 1D6x1000 credits to start as printed; the monthly salary starts at 1,900 credits plus combat pay, with room, board and clothing free. The text layer reads the dice as a cipher; confirmed 1D6x1000 and 1900 from a render. ARMOR: the book''s Special Forces Dead Boy armor is this book''s CA-7. E-clips: four for each weapon, stored as eight. The two flares are stored as signal flares. The non-energy weapon of choice is printed as typically an S.D.C. automatic weapon or a bow and arrow; the list offers catalog rows of both kinds. The vehicle for daily use is prose, as the Side Kick RPA does; see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F3. Streetwise is printed at +16%, an unusual figure, and transcribed as printed. THE ENTRY PRINTS NO BONUS LINE; the bonuses block is absent because the book gives none."
