## Lore

Special Forces are the elite of the Coalition''s fighting troops. Beyond the
commando''s espionage, sabotage, surgical strikes and guerrilla training, each
operative carries a specialty - communications, mechanics, rogue skills and
the like - which gives a team unusual range. They also serve in reaction units
that put down uprisings and threats to internal security.

They run long-range patrols and covert missions deep in enemy territory for
long stretches with little support, sometimes with no official record, and may
be sent alone, in pairs or in groups of four to six, or seeded into other units.

## GM Notes

Like Rangers, Special Forces operatives often make temporary alliances with
D-bees, mercenaries, bandits and even practitioners of magic in the field, but
they are far less tolerant than Rangers and tend to cut such ties when the
mission ends - sometimes by betraying or killing their one-time comrades, most
often someone who crossed them or deserved it. Many keep loose contacts among
nonhumans, mercenaries and outlaws.

The division has its own uniform, insignia and a more sinister skull-faced
Dead Boy armor, plus a black Special Forces SAMAS. The IAR-Hellraiser was
designed with Special Forces, Commandos and RPA Aces in mind.

On assignment: any armor, explosives if the operative knows demolitions, any
weapon and ammunition, optics, cameras, surveillance and sensory gear, weeks of
rations, and non-regulation weapons, armor and vehicles for disguise and
infiltration. Clearance runs mid to high, highest for trusted senior officers.
